<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia 97/98 barley output to fall 13 pct-ABARE.</title>
<headline>Australia 97/98 barley output to fall 13 pct-ABARE.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's barley production in 1997/98 is forecast to fall by almost 13 percent to 5.798 million tonnes, the Australian Bureau of Agricultural and Resource Economics (ABARE) said in its latest Australian Crop Report.</p>
<p>A decrease of almost 130,000 hectares sown to barley, to 3.1 million hectare, reflected a decline in barley prices relative to other crops, it said.</p>
<p>The lower production report was based on assumed average yields, it said.  </p>
<p>Australia produced 6.632 million tonnes of barley in 1996/97 (July-June).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
